UPSTREAM SOURCES AND THEIR OWN TERMS
------------------------------------
This database is derived from public sources, each of which carries its own terms. Attributing
TopPDBLX does not discharge any obligation to those sources.

  Protein Data Bank (RCSB)   The primary source of every condition string and sequence. PDB
                             data are released to the public domain (CC0 1.0). Please cite
                             the PDB alongside this work.
  SIFTS (EMBL-EBI)           PDB to UniProt residue mapping, CC BY 4.0.
  UniProt                    Reference sequences, CC BY 4.0.
  TargetTrack (Zenodo)       Archived PSI target status, acquired but not used in Phase 0.

COMMERCIAL SCREEN FORMULATIONS
------------------------------
`ontology/screens/` is a transcription of crystallisation screen formulations published by
their vendors, principally Hampton Research, extracted from the vendors' own publicly
available support materials. Formulations are published facts and citing the originator is
normal scholarly practice, but that directory is deliberately kept structurally separable:
it can be removed without breaking the rest of the release, and nothing else in the pipeline
fails if it is absent.

Screen names and product codes are trademarks of their respective owners. Their use here is
nominative, to identify the formulation being referred to, and implies no endorsement.
